# S-04 — Customer OTP identity (#16–#20, /dev/sms). Result 30 Sep 2026: all as expected.
# 202 request · 400 otp.invalid attemptsLeft=4 · 200 verify (isNew, t3s_rt Path=/v1/auth HttpOnly Secure)
# refresh 200 · old cookie <20 s 409 auth.refresh_race · after 20 s 401 auth.refresh_reused (family revoked,
# current cookie then also 401) · foreign Origin 403 http.origin_forbidden · logout-all 401 without bearer /
# 204 · 4th code in 15 min 429 otp.rate_limited retryAfterSeconds · 400 otp.mobile_invalid · code never logged.
@base = http://localhost:5080
@mobile = 0551230001

### #16 Request a code → 202 {"expiresInSeconds":300}
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}", "locale": "ar" }

### Read the code from the SMS sink (Development/Staging only)
GET {{base}}/dev/sms?count=1

### #17 Wrong code → 400 otp.invalid with attemptsLeft
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}", "code": "000000" }

### #17 Verify → 200 session + Set-Cookie t3s_rt (replace the code)
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/otp/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "mobile": "{{mobile}}", "code": "123456" }

### #18 Refresh with the cookie → 200 + rotated cookie; replaying a rotated cookie after 20 s → 401 auth.refresh_reused
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/refresh

### #19 Logout → 204, cookie cleared
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/logout

### #19 Foreign origin → 403 http.origin_forbidden
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/logout
Origin: https://evil.example

### #20 Sign out everywhere → 204 (401 auth.unauthenticated without a bearer)
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/logout-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Invalid mobile → 400 otp.mobile_invalid
POST {{base}}/v1/auth/otp/request
Content-Type: application/json
Accept-Language: en

{ "mobile": "12345" }
